.TH STORMBYTE-STAGEMANAGER 1 "August 2026" "StormByte" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
StormByte-StageManager \- manage Gentoo stage tarballs, chroots, caches and downloads
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B StormByte-StageManager
[\fICOMMAND\fR] [\fIARGS\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B StormByte-StageManager
manages Gentoo stage3 (and similar) environments stored as compressed tarballs.
It can list stages, enter a chroot, rebase into a new filename, recompress or
export stages, delete or rename them, download official stage3 images, and
attach free-form notes.
.PP
Temporary work is performed under a configurable storage backend
.RB ( folder ,
.BR tmpfs ,
or
.BR zram ).
Optional bind mounts expose host package caches, distfiles, repositories,
Portage patches and extra paths inside the chroot.
.PP
Optional
.B ccache
and
.B sccache
support can use either a host bind mount or a packed sidecar
.RI ( ccache.tbz2
/
.IR sccache.tbz2 )
under
.BR TARBALL_FOLDER .
In
.B FILE
mode the sidecar is expanded into a
.B shared tmpfs
workspace so several concurrent
.B use
/
.B rebase
sessions can share the same hot cache; the
.B last
session to exit packs the workspace back into the sidecar
.B even if
the user declines saving stage changes.
.PP
Inside the chroot, cache environment is injected transparently
.RB ( CCACHE_DIR ,
.BR FEATURES+=ccache ,
.BR SCCACHE_DIR ,
and related variables) without writing files into the stage tree.
.PP
Configuration is read from
.I StormByte-StageManager.conf
next to the script, or from
.IR /etc/conf.d/StormByte-StageManager.conf .
.SH CONFIGURATION
.TP
.I /etc/conf.d/StormByte-StageManager.conf
Primary system-wide configuration file. A copy next to the executable is also
accepted (same layout the script searches at startup).
.PP
Main variables:
.TP
.B TARBALL_FOLDER
Absolute path where stage tarballs are stored.
.TP
.B STORAGE_SYSTEM
.BR folder ,
.BR tmpfs ,
.BR zram ,
or
.B auto
(try zram, then tmpfs, then folder). Explicit values are preferred when set.
.TP
.B STORAGE_SIZE
Size for
.B tmpfs
/
.B zram
(e.g.
.BR 20G ,
.BR 512M ).
Also used as the default size for shared FILE cache tmpfs workspaces when
.B CCACHE_TMPFS_SIZE
/
.B SCCACHE_TMPFS_SIZE
are unset.
.TP
.B STORAGE_SYSTEM_ZRAM_COMPRESSION_ALGO
Optional zram algorithm:
.BR zstd ,
.BR lz4 ,
or
.BR lz4hc .
Leave empty to leave the kernel default.
.TP
.B TARBALL_NOTE_EDITOR
Editor used by
.BR "notes edit" .
.TP
.B DETACH_NOTE_EDITOR
.B YES
to background the editor (useful for GUI editors),
.B NO
otherwise.
.TP
.B GZIP_COMPRESSION_LEVEL\fR / \fBBZIP_COMPRESSION_LEVEL\fR / \fBXZ_COMPRESSION_LEVEL
Integer
.B 1
to
.BR 9 .
.TP
.B ZSTD_COMPRESSION_LEVEL
Integer
.B 1
to
.BR 19 .
.SS Compiler caches (ccache / sccache)
.TP
.B USE_CCACHE
.B YES
or
.BR NO .
If
.BR YES ,
exactly one of
.B USE_CCACHE_BIND
or
.B USE_CCACHE_FILE
must be
.BR YES .
.TP
.B CCACHE_DIR
Path used as the cache directory inside the stage (and as the host path when
.BR USE_CCACHE_BIND=YES ).
.TP
.B USE_CCACHE_BIND
Bind-mount the host
.B CCACHE_DIR
into the stage. Concurrent sessions share the host directory directly.
.TP
.B USE_CCACHE_FILE
Use the packed sidecar
.I TARBALL_FOLDER/ccache.tbz2
via a shared tmpfs workspace (see
.B SHARED FILE CACHE
below).
.TP
.B USE_SCCACHE
.B YES
or
.BR NO .
If
.BR YES ,
exactly one of
.B USE_SCCACHE_BIND
or
.B USE_SCCACHE_FILE
must be
.BR YES .
.TP
.B SCCACHE_DIR
Path used as the sccache directory inside the stage (and as the host path when
.BR USE_SCCACHE_BIND=YES ).
.TP
.B USE_SCCACHE_BIND
Bind-mount the host
.B SCCACHE_DIR
into the stage.
.TP
.B USE_SCCACHE_FILE
Use the packed sidecar
.I TARBALL_FOLDER/sccache.tbz2
via a shared tmpfs workspace.
.TP
.B SCCACHE_CACHE_SIZE
Maximum sccache disk budget passed into the chroot (default
.BR 20G ).
.SS Other paths and binds
.TP
.B PKG_DIR\fR / \fBUSE_PKG_BIND
Binary package directory and optional bind mount.
.TP
.B DISTFILES_DIR\fR / \fBUSE_DISTFILES_BIND
Distfiles directory and optional bind mount.
.TP
.B REPOS_DIR\fR / \fBUSE_REPOS_BIND
Gentoo repository path and optional bind mount.
.TP
.B USE_GENTOO_PATCHES_BIND
Bind
.I /etc/portage/patches
from the host when
.BR YES
and the host path exists.
.TP
.B EXTRA_BIND_MOUNT
Semicolon-separated list of absolute host paths to bind into the chroot.
Protected system roots are rejected.
.TP
.B BTRFS_CHECKSUM
Optional checksum name for virtual filesystems
.RB ( crc32c ,
.BR xxhash ,
.BR sha256 ,
.BR blake2 ).
.SH SHARED FILE CACHE
When
.B USE_CCACHE_FILE=YES
and/or
.B USE_SCCACHE_FILE=YES ,
each cache type uses a
.B shared tmpfs
workspace so multiple concurrent script instances can share one hot cache.
.PP
Default workspace roots (overridable via environment):
.TP
.B /tmp/StormByte-ccache
Shared ccache workspace
.RB ( CCACHE_SHARE_ROOT ).
.TP
.B /tmp/StormByte-sccache
Shared sccache workspace
.RB ( SCCACHE_SHARE_ROOT ).
.TP
.B /tmp/StormByte-cache-locks
Lock and holder metadata
.RB ( CACHE_LOCK_DIR ).
.PP
Lifecycle per cache type:
.IP \(bu 3
The
.B first
concurrent session creates the tmpfs (size
.B CCACHE_TMPFS_SIZE
/
.B SCCACHE_TMPFS_SIZE ,
defaulting to
.B STORAGE_SIZE
or
.BR 8G ),
unpacks the sidecar
.I .tbz2
if it exists, and records itself as a holder.
.IP \(bu 3
Later sessions join the same workspace (bind-mount into their stage tree) and
add themselves to the holder list. Coordination uses
.B flock
plus a holders file of live PIDs; dead PIDs are pruned on acquire and release.
.IP \(bu 3
On exit, each session removes itself from the holder list. The
.B last
session packs the workspace back into
.I ccache.tbz2
/
.I sccache.tbz2
and unmounts the tmpfs.
.IP \(bu 3
Packing is
.B independent
of whether the user saves stage tarball changes. Declining
.RB \(lq Save changes? \(rq
still persists compiler caches in FILE mode.
.IP \(bu 3
For sccache, the background server is stopped before any unmount (the daemon
holds open files on the cache directory).
.IP \(bu 3
Emergency cleanup on
.BR EXIT / INT / TERM / HUP
also stops sccache, drops stage-side binds, and runs the last-holder pack path
when appropriate.
.PP
Missing sidecars on first use are not an error: the workspace starts empty and
is packed on last exit.
.SH GLOBAL ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
.TP
.B DRY_RUN=1
Simulate heavy or destructive actions without applying them.
.TP
.B FORCE=1
Skip interactive
.BR Y / N
confirmations (delete, overwrite, save prompts still follow script logic where
applicable).
.TP
.B SKIP_CACHE=1
Skip shared FILE cache acquire/unpack and last-holder pack for this run
(BIND mode mounts are also skipped where the script gates on this flag).
.TP
.B TARBALL_FOLDER=\fI/path\fR
Override
.B TARBALL_FOLDER
for this run.
.TP
.B STORAGE_SYSTEM=\fIvalue\fR
Override storage backend for this run.
.TP
.B STORAGE_SIZE=\fIvalue\fR
Override size for
.B zram
/
.BR tmpfs
(and default shared cache tmpfs size).
.TP
.B CCACHE_SHARE_ROOT=\fI/path\fR
Override shared ccache tmpfs mountpoint (default
.IR /tmp/StormByte-ccache ).
.TP
.B SCCACHE_SHARE_ROOT=\fI/path\fR
Override shared sccache tmpfs mountpoint (default
.IR /tmp/StormByte-sccache ).
.TP
.B CACHE_LOCK_DIR=\fI/path\fR
Override directory for cache lock/holder files (default
.IR /tmp/StormByte-cache-locks ).
.TP
.B CCACHE_TMPFS_SIZE=\fIvalue\fR
Size of the shared ccache tmpfs (e.g.
.BR 8G ).
.TP
.B SCCACHE_TMPFS_SIZE=\fIvalue\fR
Size of the shared sccache tmpfs.
.TP
.B SCCACHE_CACHE_SIZE=\fIvalue\fR
sccache budget exported into the chroot (default
.BR 20G ).
.SH STAGE SELECTION
Commands that take a stage accept either:
.TP
.B <index>
Zero-based index as shown by
.BR list .
.TP
.B <filename>
Basename under
.BR TARBALL_FOLDER ,
or an absolute path to an existing stage file.
.PP
Recognised extensions:
.BR tar.gz ,
.BR tgz ,
.BR tar.bz2 ,
.BR tbz2 ,
.BR tar.xz ,
.BR txz ,
.BR tar.zstd ,
.BR tzd .
Sidecar files
.I ccache.tbz2
and
.I sccache.tbz2
are never listed as stages.
.SH COMPRESSION FORMATS
.TP
.B gzip
Extensions
.BR tar.gz / tgz ;
algorithm name
.BR gzip .
.TP
.B bzip2
Extensions
.BR tar.bz2 / tbz2 ;
algorithm name
.BR bzip2 .
.TP
.B xz
Extensions
.BR tar.xz / txz ;
algorithm name
.BR xz .
.TP
.B zstd
Extensions
.BR tar.zstd / tzd ;
algorithm name
.BR zstd .
.PP
Parallel tools are used when present
.RB ( pigz ,
.BR lbzip2 ,
.BR pxz ,
.BR pzstd ).
.B pv
is required for progress during extract/compress/download and FILE cache pack
paths.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS list (alias: ls)
.TP
.B list
List stages in
.B TARBALL_FOLDER
with index, size, mtime, and flags for notes and lock files.
.SS use
.TP
.B use \fI<index|filename>
Lock the stage, extract into temporary storage, apply bind mounts and optional
caches, enter an interactive chroot, then unmount, clean Portage temporary
data, optionally save the stage tarball, release shared FILE caches, and unlock.
.PP
On exit from the chroot the user is prompted to save
.B stage
changes unless
.B FORCE
or
.B DRY_RUN
alter the flow. Compiler caches in FILE mode are packed by the last concurrent
session regardless of that answer.
.PP
Optional ccache statistics are shown when
.B USE_CCACHE=YES
and
.B ccache
is available inside the stage. When sccache is enabled, its server is started
on chroot entry and stopped before unmount.
.SS rebase
.TP
.B rebase \fI<index|filename> <new_file_name>
Same workflow as
.BR use ,
but the stage save target is
.IR new_file_name
(compression is taken from its extension). Shared FILE cache behaviour matches
.BR use .
.SS convert
.TP
.B convert \fI<index|filename> <compression_format>
Extract and recompress the stage to the chosen format under
.BR TARBALL_FOLDER .
Fails if the target name already exists.
.SS export
.TP
.B export \fI<index|filename> <destination_folder> <compression_format>
Like
.BR convert ,
but writes into an existing
.IR destination_folder .
The output basename includes the current date
.RB ( YYYYMMDD ).
Overwrite requires confirmation unless
.BR FORCE=1 .
.SS delete (alias: rm)
.TP
.B delete \fI<index|filename>
Delete the stage file (and notes sidecar if present) after confirmation.
.SS rename
.TP
.B rename \fI<index|filename> <new_file_name>
Rename the stage within
.BR TARBALL_FOLDER .
Notes sidecar is renamed when present.
.SS download
.TP
.B download \fI<arch>\fR [\fIprofile\fR]
Download an official Gentoo stage3 for the given architecture and profile
(default profile:
.BR default ).
The stage info file is fetched with retries; the tarball is integrity-checked
against the remote
.B DIGESTS
file when available (SHA-512 preferred, else SHA-256).
.PP
Supported architectures and profiles match the built-in help
.RB ( "help download" ).
.SS notes
.TP
.B notes list
List stages that have a
.I .notes
sidecar.
.TP
.B notes \fI<index|filename> edit
Open notes with
.BR TARBALL_NOTE_EDITOR .
.TP
.B notes \fI<index|filename> delete
Remove the notes file for that stage.
.SS config
.TP
.B config
Print resolved configuration paths, storage backend, ccache/sccache flags,
shared workspace roots and sizes, bind mounts, compression levels and relevant
environment overrides.
.SS help
.TP
.B help
Show the built-in usage summary.
.TP
.B help \fI<command>
Detailed help for one command.
.TP
.B help compression
Document compression formats and extensions.
.TP
.B \-\-version\fR, \fB\-V
Print program name and version, then exit.
.SH LOCKING AND CLEANUP
Per-stage lock files live under
.I /tmp
as
.BI . <tarball-basename> .lock
and prevent concurrent use of the
.B same
stage tarball. Shared FILE caches intentionally allow concurrent sessions
across stages (or the same stage only if locks were removed by hand).
.PP
On
.BR EXIT ,
.BR INT ,
.B TERM
and
.BR HUP ,
the script runs an idempotent emergency cleanup: stop sccache if needed,
unmount stage-side cache binds, run last-holder shared-cache pack when this
process was a holder, recursive unmount of the temporary stage tree, optional
zram reset, removal of partial
.I .compress
sidecars, and deletion of the stage lock file.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success (including a user-aborted confirmation that takes no action).
.TP
.B 1
Usage error (missing or invalid arguments).
.TP
.B 2
Runtime failure (configuration, I/O, mount, download, or integrity check).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/conf.d/StormByte-StageManager.conf
System configuration.
.TP
.I TARBALL_FOLDER/*.tgz\fR (and other supported extensions)
Stage archives.
.TP
.I TARBALL_FOLDER/<stage>.notes
Optional free-form notes.
.TP
.I TARBALL_FOLDER/ccache.tbz2
Packed ccache sidecar when
.B USE_CCACHE_FILE=YES
(written by the last concurrent session).
.TP
.I TARBALL_FOLDER/sccache.tbz2
Packed sccache sidecar when
.B USE_SCCACHE_FILE=YES .
.TP
.I /tmp/StormByte-ccache
Default shared ccache tmpfs workspace.
.TP
.I /tmp/StormByte-sccache
Default shared sccache tmpfs workspace.
.TP
.I /tmp/StormByte-cache-locks/
Lock files and holder lists for shared FILE caches.
.TP
.I /tmp/.<stage>.lock
Per-stage lock file.
.SH DEPENDENCIES
.BR bash ,
.BR tar ,
.BR pv ,
.BR curl ,
.BR find ,
.BR flock
(from util-linux),
and at least one of the configured compressors
.RB ( gzip / pigz ,
.BR bzip2 / lbzip2 ,
.BR xz / pxz ,
.BR pzstd ).
Zram backends need
.B zramctl
and related kernel support.
Optional
.B ccache
/
.B sccache
binaries inside the stage when those features are enabled.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tar (1),
.BR chroot (1),
.BR pv (1),
.BR curl (1),
.BR ccache (1),
.BR sccache (1),
.BR flock (1),
.BR zramctl (8)
